## check: 004_eam_fs_ternary.incritic -a1e-6
## delete: 004_eam_fs_ternary.cro
## labels: regression quick nodata

# Ni-Al-H relaxed with an eam/fs potential. In eam/fs the density an atom
# sees depends on BOTH its own element and its neighbour's, and in this
# potential those cross-density tables are asymmetric (rho_ij /= rho_ji), so
# indexing them the wrong way round moves the minimum -- by about 0.15 in
# fractional coordinates here, against a test tolerance of 1e-6. A potential
# with symmetric cross densities cannot detect that error at all, and
# neither can a structure whose minimum is fixed by symmetry.
crystal
 cell 4.40 4.40 4.40 90 90 90 angstrom
 spg 1
 neq 0.2000 0.2000 0.2000 Ni
 neq 0.2000 0.7000 0.7000 Ni
 neq 0.7000 0.2000 0.7000 Ni
 neq 0.7000 0.7000 0.2200 Al
 neq 0.4500 0.4700 0.4400 H
endcrystal
edit relax eam 1d-7
write 004_eam_fs_ternary.incritic
